Package: UMET
Type: Package
Title: Utility-Based Dose Optimization Approach for Multiple-Dose Randomized Trial Designs (U-MET)
Version: 0.1.2
Author: Gina D'Angelo
Maintainer: The package maintainer is Gina D'Angelo <gina.dangelo@astrazeneca.com>
Description: U-MET compares randomized doses with a utility-based approach accounting for safety and efficacy. The approach compares two randomized doses by extending the BOIN12 approach to use the standardized utility scores in a hypothesis testing framework, where a frequentist and Bayesian inference are evaluated to compare the mean utilities across doses and identify the OBD. The U-MET package includes the approaches from the U-MET paper (D’Angelo et al. 2024). Another feature added is to check is the dose is admissible.
